# Force LF for every text file regardless of the checking-out platform's
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true checks files out as CRLF, but rustfmt/cargo fmt
# always writes LF - every formatting run then makes git see every
# formatted file as "modified" (a pure EOL flip, zero real content
# change), which was silently polluting `git status`/`git add -A`
# across this whole session's PRs. `text=auto` lets git still detect
# genuinely binary files (images, fonts) and leave them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings regardless of the checking-out
# platform's core.autocrlf setting - a CRLF-mangled shebang line breaks
# `#!/bin/sh` on any real POSIX shell (git-bash on Windows tolerates it,
# but the hook must also work if this repo is ever cloned on Linux/macOS).
*.sh text eol=lf
/.cargo-husky/hooks/* text eol=lf
